  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a 000-indexed binary string SSS of length N+1N + 1N+1, and your task is to construct an array AAA of length NNN such that:\n\n\nSX=1S_X = 1SX​=1 (for 0≤X≤N0 \\le X \\le N0≤X≤N) if and only if there exists LLL and RRR such that:\n\n1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N\nMEX(A[L,R])=XMEX(A[L, R]) = XMEX(A[L,R])=X, where A[L,R]A[L, R]A[L,R] denotes the subarray [AL,AL+1,…,AR][A_L, A_{L + 1}, \\ldots, A_R][AL​,AL+1​,…,AR​], and MEX denotes the minimum non-negative integer not present in the array.\n\n\nYou are guaranteed that:\n\n\nFor the given string SSS, there exists a valid array AAA, satisfying 0≤Ai≤N0 \\le A_i \\le N0≤Ai​≤N.\nS0=S1=1S_0 = S_1 = 1S0​=S1​=1, i.e. there exists at least one range in the array AAA with MEX of 000 and 111.\nYou are allowed to print any valid solution satisfying 0≤Ai≤N0 \\le A_i \\le N0≤Ai​≤N.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains a binary string SSS of size N+1N + 1N+1.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, a valid solution. It is guaranteed one exists for all the input cases that are given to you.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "3≤N≤1003 \\le N \\le 1003≤N≤100",
      "∣S∣=N+1|S| = N + 1∣S∣=N+1",
      "Si∈{0,1}S_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}Si​∈{0,1}",
      "S0=S1=1S_0 = S_1 = 1S0​=S1​=1",
      "The input is generated such that at least one valid array exists."
    ],
