        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : The array [0,2,0][0, 2, 0][0,2,0] has 666 subranges:\n\nL=1,R=1L = 1, R = 1L=1,R=1 : [0][0][0] has a MEX of 111.\nL=1,R=2L = 1, R = 2L=1,R=2 : [0,2][0, 2][0,2] has a MEX of 111.\nL=1,R=3L = 1, R = 3L=1,R=3 : [0,2,0][0, 2, 0][0,2,0] has a MEX of 111.\nL=2,R=2L = 2, R = 2L=2,R=2 : [2][2][2] has a MEX of 000.\nL=2,R=3L = 2, R = 3L=2,R=3 : [2,0][2, 0][2,0] has a MEX of 111.\nL=3,R=3L = 3, R = 3L=3,R=3 : [0][0][0] has a MEX of 111.\n\nThus, the occurring MEX values are only 000 and 111, as required by our binary string."
      }
